}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we find where the curve intersects the $y$-axis by solving the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3}-6{y}^{2}+9y & =0 \\\\ y({y}^{2}-6y+9) & =0 \\\\ y(y-3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =0,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $y=0$ to $y=3.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3}-6{y}^{2}+9y)=3{y}^{2}-12y+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\sqrt{1+{(3{y}^{2}-12y+9)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\sqrt{1+9({y}^{2}-4y+3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369092 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369093 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369092 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369094 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369092 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369095 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369092 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369096 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369092 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369097 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369092 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369092 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369092 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369097 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369092 1080 #uuid "523b63c5-49aa-5ac0-82a1-d662967676b4" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369093 1081 "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{3}y\\sqrt{1+9({y}^{3}-6{y}^{2}+9y)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369093 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369093 1084 #uuid "9dbcfd88-5069-5279-a1af-490a6715ad4e" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369094 1081 "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{6}y\\sqrt{1+9({y}^{