 have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the limits of integration are from ${x}_{1}=0$ to ${x}_{2}=1.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})=3{x}^{2}\\,⇒\\,{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}=9{x}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1/\\sqrt[4]{3}}{x}^{3}\\sqrt{1+9{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the substitution \n\n$$\nu=1+9{x}^{4}\\,⇒\\,\\text{d}u=36{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1/\\sqrt[4]{3}}{x}^{3}\\sqrt{1+9{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{u}(\\frac{1}{36}\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{18}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{18}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}\\,|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{27}(8-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369099 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369100 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369099 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369101 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369099 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369102 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369099 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369103 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369099 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369104 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369099 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369099 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369099 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369103 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369099 1080 #uuid "9b681114-61db-509f-8a32-55b8aa1