images/93/93eeedaad213d620382392235ac91835106dd772892c8c3e4ec74e808ae22179.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369188 1072 #uuid "5b02d1c4-7d7d-53ea-825a-e7c0df24295a" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369188 1074 "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=6$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{6}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369189 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369190 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369189 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369191 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369189 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369192 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369189 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369193 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369189 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369194 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369189 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369189 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369189 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369191 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369189 1080 #uuid "e4e6da79-a939-5e5c-a0d3-eb489cc25e8f" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369190 1081 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369190 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369190 1084 #uuid "81223159-c5d4-588d-9314-66a3a430542a" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369191 1081 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369191 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369191 1084 #uuid "b8e66f76-6ad4-5bdc-abf7-bebed8056693" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369192 1081 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369192 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369192 1084 #uuid "634bfffa-5e14-55f7-a686-f6fb8d6cec2b" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369193 1081 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369193 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369193 1084 #uuid "e31e6823-8cbb-53ae-bb81-764ac833481b" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369194 1081 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369194 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369194 1084 #uuid "99c6a89a-45a4-5739-bf2f-f0c0f3684523" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369195 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369196 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369195 1069 "q-115916" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369195 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369195 1071 "The radius of a circle is increasing. At a particular moment, the rate of increase of the area of the circle is numerically equal to two-fifths of the rate of increase of the diameter. Determine the radius of the circle at that moment." 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369195 1072 #uuid "e339d1ac-bcab-531c-b699-0f83006fb327" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369195 1074 "Let $r$  be the radius, $A$ the area, and $D$ the diameter of the circle. We wish to find $r$ at the moment when $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{2}{5}\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nTo start, let's set up an equation relating the area $A$ and the diameter $D$ of the circle. Since $D=2r$ and $A=\\pi {r}^{2},$ the relationship between $A$ and $D$ is\n\n$$\nA=\\pi {r}^{2}=\\pi {(\\frac{D}{2})}^{2}=\\frac{\\pi {D}^{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this relationship with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\pi {D}^{2}}{4}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}D}(\\frac{\\pi {D}^{2}}{4}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi D}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{2}{5}\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}D}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi D}{2} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =\\frac{\\pi D}{2} \\\\ D & =\\frac{4}{5\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, since $D=2r,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2r & =\\frac{4}{5\\pi } \\\\ r & =\\frac{2}{5\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369196 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369197 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369196 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369198 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369196 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369199 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369196 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369200 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369196 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369201 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369196 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369196 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369196 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369200 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369196 1080 #uuid "f608bf3b-049d-5f97-be30-40f52b88f5a0" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369197 1081 "\\frac{5}{\\pi }" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369197 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369197 1084 #uuid "86c05cb0-72a2-548a-84fc-