d}r}{\\text{d}t}=3.$\n\nTo start, let's write down the area formula for the circle and then differentiate it using implicit differentiation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2\\pi r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=3$ and $r=50,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =3\\cdot 2\\pi (50) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =300\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the area of the shadow is increasing at a rate of $300\\pi {\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\text{/min}.$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369203 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369204 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369203 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369205 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369203 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369206 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369203 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369207 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369203 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369208 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369203 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369203 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369203 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369207 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369203 1080 #uuid "eeed4af7-eaa1-51da-b490-f1e5ccb59baf" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369204 1081 "150\\pi {\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\text{/min}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369204 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369204 1084 #uuid "aefb571f-c2d0-5add-b0c3-7f93c1c43b9f" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369205 1081 "180\\pi {\\text{ cm}}^{