ite down the area formula for the circle and then differentiate it using implicit differentiation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2\\pi r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=7\\pi $ and $r=1,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\pi  & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2\\pi (1) \\\\ 7\\pi  & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =3.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the radius is increasing at a rate of $3.5$ centimeters per second." 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369210 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369211 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369210 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369212 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369210 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369213 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369210 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369214 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369210 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369215 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369210 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369210 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369210 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369212 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369210 1080 #uuid "2882600e-dd6b-59ca-8e2e-a290902aa712" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369211 1081 "2\\text{ cm}\\text{/s}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369211 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369211 1084 #uuid "94f771e8-4826-5b5d-8228-a990eba66454" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369212 1081 "3.5\\text{ cm}\\text{/s}" 13194139533449 