"q-126380" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369344 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369344 1071 "Find the fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of ${cos}^{2}⁡(x)$ about $x=\\pi .$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369344 1072 #uuid "8357d175-3c07-5e17-8c60-5510322c4e1f" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369344 1074 "The fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\n{P}_{4}(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(a)}{3!}(x-a)^{3}+\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(a)}{4!}(x-a)^{4}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $a=\\pi ,$ so\n\n$$\n{P}_{4}(x)=f(\\pi )+{f}^{′}(\\pi )(x-\\pi )+\\frac{{f}^{″}(\\pi )}{2!}{(x-\\pi )}^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(\\pi )}{3!}{(x-\\pi )}^{3}+\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(\\pi )}{4!}{(x-\\pi )}^{4}.\n$$\n\nSo we need to work out $f(\\pi ),$ ${f}^{′}(\\pi ),$ ${f}^{″}(\\pi ),$ ${f}^{‴}(\\pi )$ and ${f}^{(4)}(\\pi ),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={cos}^{2}⁡(x) & ⟹ &  & f(\\pi ) & ={cos}^{2}⁡(\\pi )=1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(\\pi ) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )=0 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(\\pi ) & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )=-2 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(\\pi ) & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )=0 \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(x) & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{(4)}(\\pi ) & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${P}_{4}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{4}(x) & =1+(0)(x-\\pi )+\\frac{(-2)}{2!}{(x-\\pi )}^{2}+\\frac{0}{3!}{(x-\\pi )}^{3}+\\frac{8}{4!}{(x-\\pi )}^{4} \\\\  & =1-{(x-\\pi )}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{(x-\\pi )}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369345 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369346 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369345 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369347 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369345 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369348 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369345 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369349 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369345 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369350 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369345 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369345 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369345 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369350 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369345 1080 #uuid "73e2ba67-5d42-5f72-913b-a1f2f409e1a1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369346 1081 "1-4(x-\\pi )+\\frac{1}{4}{(x-\\pi )}^{3}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369346 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369346 1084 #uuid "3bf1a15c-7739-5a01-bf68-ec2629c18ee3" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369347 1081 "1-(x-\\pi )+\\frac{1}{2}{(x-\\pi )}^{3}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369347 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369347 1084 #uuid "f838075f-6674-5600-9424-b0b22573c484" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369348 1081 "1-{(x-\\pi )}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{(x-\\pi )}^{4}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369348 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369348 1084 #uuid "9a9629e0-58dc-5de4-9c04-d8be27ff2577" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369349 1081 "1-2{(x-\\pi )}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{(x-\\pi )}^{4}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369349 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369349 1084 #uuid "e934f10e-857f-5393-b9d1-bd423300d351" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369350 1081 "1-{(x-\\pi )}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{(x-\\pi )}^{4}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369350 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369350 1084 #uuid "934c3f8c-3d94-5305-a125-3758f4fa62c3" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369351 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369352 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369351 1069 "q-126398" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369351 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369351 1071 "The fifth-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{P}_{5}(x)=1-\\frac{1}{2}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{3}+\\frac{1}{24}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{4}-\\frac{1}{96}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{5}.\n$$\n\nWhat is ${f}^{(4)}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})?$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369351 1072 #uuid "fa02782b-eacf-59d1-a89b-139ddd037f41" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369351 1074 "The coefficient of ${(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{4}$ is given by $\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{4!}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{4!} & =\\frac{1}{24} \\\\ \\frac{{f}^{(4)}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{24} & =\\frac{1}{24} \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369352 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369353 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369352 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369354 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369352 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369355 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369352 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369356 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369352 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369357 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369352 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369352 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369352 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369354 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369352 1080 #uuid "d220d03a-3e39-5391-8291-436bc9f820c9" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369353 1081 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369353 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369353 1084 #uuid "639db55a-44ef-59c9-a322-679a57879f5b" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369354 1081 "1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369354 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369354 1084 #uuid "74276d34-bbfb-52ed-bc28-7984b9b0d0f9" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369355 1081 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369355 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369355 1084 #uuid "74b9ea7f-46ae-5143-a9e5-77c260ebbffb" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369356 1081 "-\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369356 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369356 1084 #uuid "5c2ca06e-5b67-5a44-9a06-cbec8aaa6dfc" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369357 1081 "-1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369357 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369357 1084 #uuid "8847cdc7-6beb-5679-abf3-ac630967228e" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369358 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369359 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369358 1069 "q-126553" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369358 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369358 1071 "![](images/17/172a9d82a656777885ed7e9d6850e8c4e80089fcea87c9b80cd3475a8bfb1e12.png)\n\nConsider the arc of the curve $x={y}^{2}-{y}^{4}$ that lies in the first quadrant between its $y$-intercepts. What integral gives the surface area generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis?" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369358 1072 #uuid "69a8f74b-ef94-5435-816b-b323b079aba9" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369358 1074 "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi y\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $x=f(y),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we find where the curve intersects the $y$-axis by solving the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-{y}^{4} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}(1-{y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $y=0$ to $y=1.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2}-{y}^{4})=2y-4{y}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\sqrt{1+{(2y-4{y}^{3})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\sqrt{1+4{y}^{2}-16{y}^{4}+16{y}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369359 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369360 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369359 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369361 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369359 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369362 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369359 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369363 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369359 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369364 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369359 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369359 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369359 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369363 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369359 1080 #uuid "430efe42-1b12-5fd7-acc4-5da2aad79f6d" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369360 1081 "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\sqrt{1+4{y}^{2}-8{y}^{4}+8{y}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369360 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369360 1084 #uuid "b354887a-67cf-5c84-b674-1116a09b1f39" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369361 1081 "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-{y}^{4})\\sqrt{1+4{y}^{2}-16{y}^{4}+16{y}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369361 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369361 1084 #uuid "5599c132-2516-5891-8983-039c0cf22b15" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369362 1081 "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-{y}^{4})\\sqrt{1+4{y}^{2}-16{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369362 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369362 1084 #uuid "eb0408c8-424d-5552-b183-9c6d7e8abd76" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369363 1081 "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\sqrt{1+4{y}^{2}-16{y}^{4}+16{y}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369363 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369363 1084 #uuid "6b2b878c-f07b-51cc-b4b0-adafd9cfaa45" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369364 1081 "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\sqrt{1+16{y}^{4}-16{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369364 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369364 1084 #uuid "4018c268-0f5c-5134-875d-32abcfd28b24" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369365 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369366 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369365 1069 "q-126560" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369365 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369365 1071 "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the functions $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)?$\n\n- $P(x,y)={e}^{x+y}-\\frac{y}{2}$ and $Q(x,y)={e}^{x+y}+\\frac{x}{2}$\n- $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ and $Q(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- $P(x,y)=x$ and $Q(x,y)=x$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369365 1072 #uuid "cf5aefc1-27f1-5c4b-be31-6e2e9699a7da" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369365 1074 "According to Green's theorem, if \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Pair I gives the required area.  In this case,\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{x+y}-\\frac{1}{2}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={e}^{x+y}+\\frac{1}{2},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Pair II does *not* give the required area.  Notice that \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369366 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369367 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369366 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369368 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369366 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369369 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369366 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369370 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369366 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369371 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369366 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369366 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369366 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369368 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369366 1080 #uuid "5a1e341d-7570-5f89-bb15-0d2fc13ee8fe" 1319413