5499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369387 1084 #uuid "d09c91eb-6025-563c-9e1e-422c46c45a06" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369388 1081 "-2\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369388 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369388 1084 #uuid "f7db36f3-e726-57a8-990c-cb139c3421dd" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369389 1081 "3\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369389 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369389 1084 #uuid "0d9cd067-f29c-5dd2-92a7-39171feb6a4c" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369390 1081 "6\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369390 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369390 1084 #uuid "5df13d18-ed06-5111-b470-86ff1f65bc05" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369391 1081 "2\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369391 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369391 1084 #uuid "3ab6388d-f385-5685-97ba-bf84a736e56a" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369392 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369393 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369392 1069 "q-126579" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369392 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369392 1071 "Consider the arc of the curve $y=\\frac{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}{2}$ that lies between the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$ Calculate the surface area generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis." 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369392 1072 #uuid "281c9245-03d2-50f3-8052-d171994fc48c" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369392 1074 "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi y\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $y=f(x),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the limits of integration are from ${x}_{1}=0$ to ${x}_{2}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}{2})=\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{2}\\,⇒\\,{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}=\\frac{{({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})}^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\frac{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}{2})\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{({e}^{x}-{e}^{-x})}^{2}}{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\frac{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}}{2})\\sqrt{\\frac{4+{e}^{2x}-2+{e}^{-2x}}{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}+2+{e}^{-2x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})\\sqrt{{({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({e}^{2x}+2+{e}^{-2x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2x}+2x-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x}]}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})-\\frac{\\pi }{2}(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{0}+2(0)-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\pi (1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(15+16\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)\\pi }{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 1759218604