6045585 true] [17592186369426 1074 "Our simple, smooth, closed path $C$ is negatively oriented, and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNotice that we have to take the line integral with a minus sign since the path is negatively oriented.\n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x,$ we get\n\n$$\n-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y={∮}_{C}-x\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}-x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot 6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369427 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369428 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369427 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369429 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369427 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369430 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369427 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369431 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369427 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369432 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369427 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369427 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369427 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369429 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369427 1080 #uuid "f0b9dd1e-629f-5bde-86fc-a981f5b5dd34" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369428 1081 "-18\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369428 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 1