id "8b773c29-9e6f-5096-b07b-de5aaca35eab" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369433 1074 "First, let $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0.$\n\nOur simple, piecewise-smooth, closed path $C$ is positively oriented and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0-(-1)=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y=-{∮}_{C}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivatives of ${r}_{1}(t)$ and ${r}_{2}(t)$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\, & {r}_{1}^{′}(t)=-4t\\,i+9{t}^{2}\\,j \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\, & {r}_{2}^{′}(t)=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{∮}_{C}y\\,\\text{d}x & =-{∮}_{{C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}}y\\,dx \\\\  & =-{∮}_{{C}_{1}}y\\,dx-{∮}_{{C}_{2}}y\\,dx \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}3{t}^{3}\\cdot (-4t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{-3}^{3}(-t)\\cdot 0\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =12{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{t}^{4}\\,\\text{d}t-0 \\\\  & =12[\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =12\\cdot \\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369435 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369436 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369437 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369438 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369434 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369439 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369434 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369434 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369434 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369439 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369434 1080 #uuid "dbaaffb7-8edd-5da1-89b3-b92a5ba8c4dd" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369435 1081 "\\frac{4}{5}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369435 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369435 1084 #uuid "1d263f40-9c2f-5a37-bde8-f22ac722349c" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369436 1081 "\\frac{14}{3}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369436 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369436 1084 #uuid "d98084a7-8c18-5006-8eaf-808ce526a650" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369437 1081 "6" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369437 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369437 1084 #uuid "c270fb54-3408-58f5-94c5-0ccc6a0d2bb1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369438 1081 "4" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369438 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369438 1084 #uuid "89fea390-1808-5719-8411-656965ac4356" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369439 1081 "\\frac{24}{5}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369439 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369439 1084 #uuid "f90a6d10-d2f7-5146-b3e5-bd6446824220" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369440 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369441 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369440 1069 "q-126853" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369440 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369440 1071 "![](images/39/393bed476f2e8d84fc7e5dc721d77749f7f259834e03a94a48a08533ae9befa6.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}2y\\,dx+4x\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the region shown above." 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369440 1072 #uuid "32a18b85-d978-5b18-8fff-914bdccf82dc" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369440 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=2y$ and $Q(x,y)=4x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}2y\\,dx+4x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(4-2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (6\\cdot 4-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (24-4) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 20 \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369441 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369442 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369441 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369443 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369441 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369444 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369441 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369445 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369441 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369446 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369441 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369441 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369441 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369445 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369441 1080 #uuid "d2ee2d3e-bbe0-5737-8885-1738f355a09b" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369442 1081 "20" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369442 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369442 1084 #uuid "8fe866fa-6339-5f10-8ce3-3d5938c3785e" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369443 1081 "60" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] 