,y)=3y$ and $Q(x,y)=2x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=3,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}3y\\,dx+2x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2-3)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}-1\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-\\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =-(\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}-\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}) \\\\  & =-(9\\pi -\\pi ) \\\\  & =-8\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369448 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369449 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369448 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369450 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369448 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369451 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369448 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369452 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369448 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369453 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369448 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369448 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369448 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369450 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369448 1080 #uuid "37fee2c5-b026-5dca-a84d-1a957d12aae4" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369449 1081 "9\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369449 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369449 1084 #uuid "992dce16-160e-53f6-8630-c0af64cae1cb" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369450 1081 "-8\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369450 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369450 1084 #uuid "2bfd9130-7a02-5b45-a0d5-85f79505dd79" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369451 1081 "-12\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369451 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369451 1084 #uuid "2ce07f1c-821c-51aa-8553-62af6bab118d" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369452 1081 "10\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369452 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369452 1084 #uuid "905e612c-8067-5089-bf8b-dc0ca7481414" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369453 1081 "6\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369453 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369453 1084 #uuid "bae5a3fa-eb19-574d-b4eb-7f975d579bd1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369454 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369455 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369454 1069 "q-126858" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369454 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369454 1071 "![](images/52/52ec0dfc4590daf9306c2389bd321acbf80f263c799fa4ddd4e5b8f662e0a2b5.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2},$ where \n\n- ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(t)={t}^{5}\\,i+{t}^{4}\\,j$ for $t\\in [-1,1],$ and\n\n- ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(t)=-t\\,i+1\\,j$ for $t\\in [-1,1].$\n\nUse Green's theorem to find the area of the region." 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369454 1072 #uuid "7834afec-6e2d-5917-b360-ab0e90141806" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369454 1074 "First, let $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x.$\n\nOur simple, piecewise-smooth, closed path $C$ is positively oriented and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x,$ we get\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y={∮}_{C}x\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivatives of ${r}_{1}(t)$ and ${r}_{2}(t)$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\, & {r}_{1}^{′}(t)=5{t}^{4}\\,i+4{t}^{3}\\,j \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\, & {r}_{2}^{′}(t)=-i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}}x\\,dy \\\\  & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}x\\,dy+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}x\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{t}^{5}\\cdot 4{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-t)\\cdot 0\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{t}^{8}\\,\\text{d}t-0 \\\\  & =4[\\frac{{t}^{9}}{9}]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{2}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369455 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369456 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369455 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369457 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369455 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369458 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369455 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369459 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369455 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369460 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369455 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369455 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369455 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369457 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369455 1080 #uuid "f29d4169-0dcc-5881-9d8b-1107b9cc1f1c" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369456 1081 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369456 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369456 1084 #uuid "1bd2f859-8cbd-5fb2-a799-4047912f2b9b" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369457 1081 "\\frac{8}{9}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369457 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369457 1084 #uuid "c80ede24-c0d9-5ecf-be0b-3875c8087b10" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369458 1081 "4" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369458 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369458 1084 #uuid "b67159a4-a2c9-5c6e-a51b-b9e8fec0e05d" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369459 1081 "\\frac{5}{4}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369459 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369459 1084 #uuid "6d280bef-8091-5d89-be52-181cdb57aaa5" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369460 1081 "5" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369460 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369460 1084 #uuid "aa5c20b2-9d53-5d85-af6f-b027ed46706b" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369461 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369462 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369461 1069 "q-126860" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369461 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369461 1071 "![](images/b5/b5a42039e2501a3909062fd6ed92e0879df03f58fa85a62b5e738e8abc78b903.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}8x\\,dy-5y\\,dx,$ where $D$ is the region shown above." 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369461 1072 #uuid "017f8f34-6e37-562a-87cf-df5a06a7e434" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369461 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=-5y$ and $Q(x,y)=8x.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-5,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}8x\\,dy-5y\\,dx & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(8-(-5))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}13\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =13{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =13\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =13\\cdot ({8}^{2}-{6}^{2}) \\\\  & =13\\cdot (64-36) \\\\  & =13\\cdot 28 \\\\  & =364.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369462 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369463 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369462 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369464 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369462 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369465 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369462 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369466 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369462 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369467 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369462 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369462 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369462 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369463 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369462 1080 #uuid "175c17d1-364f-5ab7-a6b1-2ce4de237b97" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369463 1081 "364" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369463 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369463 1084 #uuid "74b43056-e8dd-536d-b56a-12ac2800c12b" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369464 1081 "215" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369464 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369464 1084 #uuid "ca09836f-3c6e-5b5f-841d-68ede18363c7" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369465 1081 "424" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369465 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369465 1084 #uuid "ac3caf47-5329-54b1-8c87-bcf0da3ef96b" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369466 1081 "342" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369466 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369466 1084 #uuid "b9b5b1dc-7bc7-5bb9-8b23-063bc496f471" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369467 1081 "124" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369467 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 