ion $D$ above. Given that \n\n$$\n{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=5,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-2,\\,{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-9,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are oriented clockwise and ${C}_{3}$ is oriented counterclockwise, calculate the value of ${∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369496 1072 #uuid "d9bfcd0d-e2e4-5ddd-944e-eb308c18a16d" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369496 1074 "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/2b/2bed1b367cd101e0e90674c619ad87da8c90744df570eeea4d9b0333ccee0de1.png)\n\nNotice that the positive orientations of the outer curve ${C}_{1}$ and the inner curve ${C}_{3}$ are opposite those stated in the question.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & =-{∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-5+(-2)-(-9) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369497 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369498 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369497 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369497 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369500 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369497 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369501 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369497 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369502 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369497 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369497 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369497 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369501 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369497 1080 #uuid "998a54d8-ef67-567f-aff6-05f6543bcc9b" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369498 1081 "12" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369498 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369498 1084 #uuid "19b2f076-3c1b-5b41-b54d-acbf22c85f9b" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369499 1081 "-16" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369499 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369499 1084 #uuid "dcf840d4-a3b7-5a1f-8ab9-000eaa11d729" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369500 1081 "16" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369500 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369500 1084 #uuid "544f331d-d37a-57d2-a8ec-3849a346d73c" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369501 1081 "2" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369501 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369501 1084 #uuid "7953c459-d75a-5d7a-a051-42cf152ae33e" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369502 1081 "6" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369502 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369502 1084 #uuid "fc7aedd6-9474-596f-83c6-b28c824b5114" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369503 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369504 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369503 1069 "q-126894" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369503 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369503 1071 "![](images/0e/0e86380c457bc9d37d0180057d4ce8c035055986d32254d95fab3a69254531a5.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}6y\\,dx+9x\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the annular region shown above." 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369503 1072 #uuid "c3c22304-91b2-51e6-94d5-71e3689e1379" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369503 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=6y$ and $Q(x,y)=9x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=6,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}dx+x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(9-6)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3\\,\\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}-\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 5\\pi  \\\\  & =15\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369504 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369505 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369504 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369506 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369504 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369507 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369504 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369508 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369504 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369509 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369504 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369504 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369504 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369507 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369504 1080 #uuid "4a4245ec-3053-53c4-bb04-e49df5e84b57" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369505 1081 "12\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369505 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369505 1084 #uuid "5e6750b8-75e8-5604-bdf3-5b26e689ff79" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369506 1081 "14\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369506 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369506 1084 #uuid "71c2554d-1b8f-50ee-904e-bf572ea954dc" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369507 1081 "15\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369507 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369507 1084 #uuid "d3d1e293-45b2-553f-8738-81af539d167d" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369508 1081 "16\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369508 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369508 1084 #uuid "808c516e-8fb0-5d9d-b3c3-71bd5e0c0d18" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369509 1081 "18\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369509 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369509 1084 #uuid "56bd1130-5922-503b-9779-186620077dd1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369510 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369511 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369510 1069 "q-126935" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369510 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369510 1071 "![](images/5c/5ca9f071eaeebb0b31fba99a48ca8f08bd6b4b73588838aad7b5f513c283fd6c.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}-({x}^{4}y+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}{y}^{3})\\,dx+(x{y}^{4}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}{y}^{2})\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the annular region shown above." 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369510 1072 #uuid "a38e1386-54d8-53c8-80be-ec42c2b70086" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369510 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=-{x}^{4}y-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}$ and $Q(x,y)=x{y}^{4}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={y}^{4}+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}-({x}^{4}y+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}{y}^{3})\\,dx+(x{y}^{4}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}{y}^{2})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{4}+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-(-{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 3,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nRecall that the change of variables formula for polar coordinates gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, our double integral becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{3}((r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2})^{2}\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{3}{r}^{4}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{3}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta {\\int }_{1}^{3}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{3}{r}^{5}\\,\\text{d}r \\\\  & =2\\pi \\cdot {\\frac{1}{6}{r}^{6}|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\cdot ({3}^{6}-{1}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{728\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369511 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369512 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369511 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369513 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369511 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369514 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369511 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369515 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369511 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369516 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369511 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369511 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369511 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369514 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369511 1080 #uuid "0fe2c0c3-ccf0-5837-bf7d-eba354f732ab" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369512 1081 "\\frac{80\\pi }{3}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369512 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369512 1084 #uuid "f6a80b35-ba1d-5225-b811-45d42e3518c3" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369513 1081 "\\frac{242\\pi }{3}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369513 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369513 1084 #uuid "e3d29cd2-757a-5f31-a966-786ef1201ef4" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369514 1081 "\\frac{728\\pi }{3}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369514 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369514 1084 #uuid "9a7bf771-68a8-5635-b443-270be3859a67" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369515 1081 "728\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369515 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369515 1084 #uuid "3d1b880d-8ca7-5039-a151-5e9c415014b0" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369516 1081 "243\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369516 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369516 1084 #uuid "db63a2b7-a407-5f7d-b9b2-4abcfc16c974" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369517 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369518 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369517 1069 "q-126937" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369517 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369517 1071 "![](images/e6/e6252037001e1a5548ede86a16b4ddde8f5aec8fd956bded55a3506f7b533dbe.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}(\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({sin}^{2}⁡y)-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the annular region shown above." 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369517 1072 #uuid "88b73727-8c06-5f8a-b431-35e41d39a38b" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369517 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $Q(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({sin}^{2}⁡y)-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}(\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,dx+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({sin}^{2}⁡y)-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,2\\le r\\le 4,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nRecall that the change of variables formula for polar coordinates gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, our double integral becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{2}^{4}-((r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2})\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{2}^{4}-{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{2}^{4}-{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta {\\int }_{2}^{4}-{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r \\\\  & =-2\\pi {\\int }_{2}^{4}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r \\\\  & =-2\\pi \\cdot {\\frac{1}{4}{r}^{4}|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot ({4}^{4}-{2}^{4}) \\\\  & =-120\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369518 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369519 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369518 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369520 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369518 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369521 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369518 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369522 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369518 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369523 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369518 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369518 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369518 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369522 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369518 1080 #uuid "1d326558-bc4e-5ef3-84ac-5f28a471d7e6" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369519 1081 "-90\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369519 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369519 1084 #uuid "adb00ccb-3eb2-54ed-b39e-a1b797a275e5" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369520 1081 "120\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369520 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369520 1084 #uuid "7353f729-db5d-5849-9168-5e4b921191db" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369521 1081 "-145\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369521 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369521 1084 #uuid "f2684cd6-1f99-5ede-94b6-e3ceba6e28d2" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369522 1081 "-120\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369522 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369522 1084 #uuid "f2d8e429-0275-503d-8cb9-59c096c6a40c" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369523 1081 "90\\pi " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369523 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369523 1084 #uuid "1b918db5-2ba3-5ac0-8eae-fc4b0f13cbc5" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369524 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369525 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369524 1069 "q-126941" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369524 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369524 1071 "![](images/b2/b232a4cddf05a425709c1b3204b69b0126e586b42a6af73b867dd75ee294d961.png)\n\nCalculate \n${∮}_{∂D}({x}^{3}{y}^{3}+x)\\,dx+({x}^{4}{y}^{2}-y)\\,dy,$\nwhere $D$ is the region shown above." 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369524 1072 #uuid "ae4fa615-3a59-509f-96cf-981693bf3db2" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369524 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)={x}^{3}{y}^{3}+x$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{4}{y}^{2}-y.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=3{x}^{3}{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=4{x}^{3}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}({x}^{3}{y}^{3}+x)\\,dx+({x}^{4}{y}^{2}-y)\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}4{x}^{3}{y}^{2}-3{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be represented in Cartesian coordinates as ${Δ}_{1}∖{Δ}_{2},$ where\n\n- ${Δ}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,-1\\le y\\le 2}$ is the region enclosed by the outer curve, and\n\n- ${Δ}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,0\\le y\\le 1}$ is the region enclosed by the inner curve.\n\nTherefore, our double integral becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{{Δ}_{1}}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A-{∬}_{{Δ}_{2}}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}\\,{|}_{-2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}\\,{|}_{-1}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(4-4)\\cdot (\\frac{8}{3}-(-\\frac{1}{3}))-(\\frac{1}{4}-0)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}-0) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 3-\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369525 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369526 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369525 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369527 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369525 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369528 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369525 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369529 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369525 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369530 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369525 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369525 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369525 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369526 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369525 1080 #uuid "38c1ef24-72d4-585c-9c7b-034e01ca1112" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369526 1081 "-\\frac{1}{12}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369526 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369526 1084 #uuid "9d05767d-a65e-5d43-a488-57f4105f6090" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369527 1081 "-\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369527 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369527 1084 #uuid "b9437141-8677-5d36-ade8-56553767eb3c" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369528 1081 "0" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369528 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369528 1084 #uuid "71c53a26-6b18-5e5a-a6b4-14d20c2a1939" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369529 1081 "-\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369529 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369529 1084 #uuid "c90c6307-93a1-5a42-b489-784db15ed739" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369530 1081 "-1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369530 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369530 1084 #uuid "d963956c-f4e3-525a-b6b9-91fd86eb5922" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369531 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369532 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369531 1069 "q-126945" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369531 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369531 1071 "![](images/75/754aa1ded10b20362350f3da9e5b4dbe5f9f194c2289af348ff9de34f2fb8cc5.png)\n\nCalculate \n${∮}_{∂D}(x{y}^{2}+{x}^{3})\\,dx+(2{x}^{2}y-{y}^{3})\\,dy,$\nwhere $D$ is the region shown above." 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369531 1072 #uuid "904872cd-e02c-55d9-9792-17de482b0907" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369531 1074 "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=x{y}^{2}+{x}^{3}$ and $Q(x,y)=2{x}^{2}y-{y}^{3}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2xy,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=4xy.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}(x{y}^{2}+{x}^{3})\\,dx+(2{x}^{2}y-{y}^{3})\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}4xy-2xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be represented in Cartesian coordinates as ${Δ}_{1}∖{Δ}_{2},$ where\n\n- ${Δ}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,-1\\le y\\le 2}$ is the region enclosed by the outer curve, and\n\n- ${Δ}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,0\\le y\\le 1}$ is the region enclosed by the inner curve.\n\nTherefore, our double integral becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{{Δ}_{1}}2xy\\,\\text{d}A-{∬}_{{Δ}_{2}}2xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}2xy\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}2xy\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}2x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{-1}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}2x\\,\\text{d}x{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\,{|}_{-2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{-1}^{2}-{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{-1}^{1}\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(4-4)\\cdot (2-\\frac{1}{2})-(1-1)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}-0\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369532 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369533 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369532 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369534 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369532 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369535 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369532 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369536 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369532 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369537 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369532 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369532 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369532 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369537 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369532 1080 #uuid "1303c02b-a3ee-52e9-98a2-763dbec18e4b" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369533 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369533 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369533 1084 #uuid "006e746d-7483-59b3-ba9c-8cd280691f9d" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369534 1081 "-\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369534 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369534 1084 #uuid "64fc0003-b805-567e-8d14-5ab416216a60" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369535 1081 "1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369535 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369535 1084 #uuid "14561ae1-e3be-5f9d-bccd-fde3e73d6059" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369536 1081 "-\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369536 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369536 1084 #uuid "da7adf00-3485-5b42-ac23-7efeb71d22ab" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369537 1081 "0" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369537 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369537 1084 #uuid "89cc8f37-3c67-5183-a3bc-6cf27168df13" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369538 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369539 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369538 1069 "q-127007" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369538 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369538 1071 "Which of the following functions satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[-4,0]?$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369538 1072 #uuid "54c890b5-4ccb-5b1b-899e-441e17682cb7" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369538 1074 "For a function to satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[-4,0],$ the function must be continuous on $[-4,0]$ and differentiable on $(-4,0).$\n\nFirst, notice that the function $v(x)$ is continuous on $[-4,0]$ and differentiable on $(-4,0),$ so it satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nLet's check each of the other functions individually.\n\n- The function $r(x)$ is continuous on $[-4,0]$ but has a corner point at $x=-1.$ Hence, $r(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=-1,$ which means it is not differentiable on $(-4,0).$ Therefore, $r(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $s(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=-2.$ Hence, $s(x)$ is not continuous on $[-4,0].$ Therefore, $s(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $t(x)$ is continuous on $[-4,0]$ but has a corner point at $x=-2.$ Hence, $t(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=-2,$ which means it is not differentiable on $(-4,0).$ Therefore, $t(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $u(x)$  has a vertical asymptote at $x=-1.$ Hence, $u(x)$ is not continuous on $[-4,0].$ Therefore, $u(x)$ does not satisfiy the conditions of the mean value theorem." 13194139533449 17592186045