4139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369544 1081 "images/58/58a90a39e3bdaa433e6bc2f4592ba7d75c9bdb318db9705aae02b3c55d86a593.png" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369544 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369544 1084 #uuid "b29c7e9e-a79b-501f-8e4e-2daac657f7ef" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369545 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369546 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369545 1069 "q-127774" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369545 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369545 1071 "Consider the following game featuring two fair six-sided dice rolled simultaneously. If the sum of the numbers on the dice is $6,$ the player wins $$6.$ Otherwise, the player loses $$1.$ What is the expected profit from each roll in this game? Round your answer to three decimal places." 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369545 1072 #uuid "3b5495b2-a94a-588d-89ee-34582e5049ee" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369545 1074 "Let $p$ represent the profit on a single roll of the game. On each roll in the game, there are two possible outcomes:\n\n- If the sum of the outcomes is $6$ ($(1,5),(2,4),(3,3),(4,2)$, or $(5,1)$), the player wins $$6,$ so we have $p=6.$\n\n- If the sum of the outcomes is not $6,$ the player loses $$1,$ so we have $p=-1.$\n\nThe probabilities for the outcomes are\n\n$$\nP(6)=\\frac{5}{36},\\,P(-1)=\\frac{31}{36}.\n$$\n\nLet's summarize this in a table. If $p$ is the profit (in dollars) on a single game, and $f(p)$ is the probability mass function for $p,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $f(p)$ | $\\frac{5}{36}$ | $\\frac{31}{36}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $p$ | $6$ | $-1$ |\n\nTherefore, the expected value of $p$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E[p] & =6\\cdot f(6)+(-1)\\cdot f(-1) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{5}{36})+(-1)(\\frac{31}{36}) \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{36}-\\frac{31}{36} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{36} \\\\  & ≈-0.028\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected profit is $-$0.028.$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369547 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369548 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369549 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369550 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369546 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369551 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369546 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369546 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369546 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369549 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369546 1080 #uuid "083ca59a-ef03-5bb8-86e1-785f85c590ff" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369547 1081 "$$0.028$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369547 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369547 1084 #uuid "a2441b13-5d85-5de5-92df-ad5d613f68e7" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369548 1081 "$-$2.812$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369548 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369548 1084 #uuid "3f302c6b-b6a7-5a5e-a56c-9260199538b0" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369549 1081 "$-$0.028$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369549 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369549 1084 #uuid "d592d39d-b18e-5066-8c17-d6d2aa7992c6" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369550 1081 "$-$0.28$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369550 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369550 1084 #uuid "891a5c79-b343-5003-ac71-aa61a11b9936" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369551 1081 "$$0.28$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369551 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369551 1084 #uuid "d