7592186045585 true] [17592186369636 1074 "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+3\\cdot f(3)+5\\cdot f(5)+7\\cdot f(7)+9\\cdot f(9) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{5})+3(\\frac{1}{3})+5(\\frac{2}{15})+7(\\frac{4}{15})+9(\\frac{1}{15}) \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{5}^{2}\\cdot f(5)+{7}^{2}\\cdot f(7)+{9}^{2}\\cdot f(9) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{5})+9(\\frac{1}{3})+25(\\frac{2}{15})+49(\\frac{4}{15})+81(\\frac{1}{15}) \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =25-{(\\frac{13}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =25-\\frac{169}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{225}{9}-\\frac{169}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{56}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369637 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369638 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369637 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369639 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369637 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369640 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369637 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369641 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369637 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369642 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369637 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369637 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369637 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369640 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369637 1080 #uuid "a25f0f69-2aea-5e91-8812-1596673e1194" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369638 1081 "\\frac{56}{3}" 131