\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a diagonal matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}| & ={(\\sqrt{3})}^{4}=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\text{det}(A)-\\text{det}(\\sqrt{3}I)=6-9=-3.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. We have\n\n$$\n2\\text{det}({A}^{T})+\\text{det}(\\sqrt{3}I)=2\\cdot 6+9=21.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. We have, \n\n$$\n\\text{det}({A}^{T})+2\\text{det}(\\sqrt{3}I)=6+2\\cdot 9=24.\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369707 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369708 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369707 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369709 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369707 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369710 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369707 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369711 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369707 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369712 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369707 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369707 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369707 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369708 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369707 1080 #uuid "886196d8-179f-5894-8b4b-8a7bab9be29a" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369708 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369708 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369708 1084 #uuid "f1edde84-d8d9-5d8c-991a-dac8766db6cd" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [1759218