ue] [17592186369866 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369871 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369866 1080 #uuid "527d4c6b-012b-5461-8a47-41cb9dad1d47" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369867 1081 "8" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369867 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369867 1084 #uuid "5fa62dd2-b0c7-5d84-9d22-decbfe7c3d62" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369868 1081 "2" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369868 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369868 1084 #uuid "9a2809d5-b0a6-5909-8b19-67d21b2cf85d" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369869 1081 "6" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369869 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369869 1084 #uuid "5acf1a1f-a6ef-514f-8acc-ff08cda8690f" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369870 1081 "1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369870 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369870 1084 #uuid "a4fd4552-6bd6-501b-be53-4c059be4aaf1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369871 1081 "4" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369871 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369871 1084 #uuid "9ea75817-ef2f-5f2f-9943-1818c631b13b" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369872 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369873 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369872 1069 "q-158448" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369872 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369872 1071 "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}k{x}^{4}+x,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369872 1072 #uuid "c0521bf1-bd8f-5dae-afd2-d396563ae145" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369872 1074 "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nFor the given function, the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}(k{x}^{4}+x)\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(k{x}^{4}+x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{k{x}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{k}{5}+\\frac{1}{2}]-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{5}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{k}{5}+\\frac{1}{2}=1\\,⟹\\,k=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369873 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369874 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369873 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369875 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369873 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369876 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369873 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369877 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369873 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369878 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369873 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369873 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369873 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369874 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369873 1080 #uuid "2a48ce47-1dde-5165-92d6-df0d9be50c48" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369874 1081 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369874 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369874 1084 #uuid "e87225b8-c68e-5d26-891e-cbfd70d2a34e" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369875 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369875 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369875 1084 #uuid "84e9ce82-ac12-54ad-9778-57500a3d8cfe" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369876 1081 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369876 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369876 1084 #uuid "ebf8b546-cf03-5c3b-bcf4-accde6fe6516" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369877 1081 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369877 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369877 1084 #uuid "e8e75ee4-9dca-5c87-a673-14e5f8c71af6" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369878 1081 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369878 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369878 1084 #uuid "9fbfdf2c-16f2-5ec3-8602-e28b2c6c74a3" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369879 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369880 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369879 1069 "q-160445" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369879 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369879 1071 "For the transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u \\\\ -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ncompute the value of the Jacobian determinant at the point where $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\pi /4 \\\\ \\pi /4\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369879 1072 #uuid "91c905cb-29ef-5cbc-a791-764e51ba7eed" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369879 1074 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u$ and $y(u,v)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡v.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)-0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\pi /4 \\\\ \\pi /4\\end{aligned}],$ the value of our Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n{\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4})}=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=3.\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369880 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369881 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369880 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369882 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369880 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369883 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369880 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369884 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369880 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369885 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369880 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369880 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369880 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369881 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369880 1080 #uuid "c478e331-2d1a-585a-9599-198d7061ae49" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369881 1081 "3" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369881 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369881 1084 #uuid "4dc0ac04-220f-5368-899c-f4b853d6caf1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369882 1081 "2" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369882 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369882 1084 #uuid "f515d3db-880a-5d23-99f0-9cb65e633ebf" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369883 1081 "6" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369883 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369883 1084 #uuid "57254211-1cc3-5a7f-87e1-0c345d6ba0b6" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369884 1081 "4" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369884 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369884 1084 #uuid "0ab4227a-a1c7-56de-9a4e-de04cc753871" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369885 1081 "-6" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369885 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369885 1084 #uuid "47ca5fb3-37c5-5519-9b75-0484cfdf1808" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369886 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369887 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369886 1069 "q-161201" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369886 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369886 1071 "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with unit normal vector $n,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨{x}^{2}+{y}^{2},\\,xz,\\,z+{y}^{2}⟩\\,,\\,n(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩\\,.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{∬}_{S}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369886 1072 #uuid "6c94dc83-cb78-54c3-8e1e-5cf36cded66a" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369886 1074 "If $S$ is an oriented surface with unit normal vector $n,$ and $F$ is continuous vector field, then the flux of $F$ across $S$ measured with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nCalculating the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨{x}^{2}+{y}^{2},\\,xz,\\,z+{y}^{2}⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨{x}^{2}+{y}^{2},\\,xz,\\,z+{y}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})+0-(z+{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-z}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\frac{{x}^{2}-z}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{∬}_{S}{x}^{2}-z\\,\\text{d}S.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369887 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369888 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369887 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369889 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369887 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369890 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369887 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369891 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369887 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369892 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369887 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369887 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369887 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369888 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369887 1080 #uuid "4b0fb886-3e02-5fa7-af49-6e0fc64fadf4" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369888 1081 "{x}^{2}-z" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369888 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369888 1084 #uuid "4db4d76a-1cbf-546e-9910-5eefab212094" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369889 1081 "{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369889 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369889 1084 #uuid "93b13355-74c7-5944-8894-d63214e49d4e" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369890 1081 "2{y}^{2}+xz-z" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369890 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369890 1084 #uuid "ad64ad66-1217-56c6-9f34-a805076c7edc" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369891 1081 "{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-z" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369891 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369891 1084 #uuid "dd863173-56c4-5d31-b3b2-62ef6fc703dd" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369892 1081 "{x}^{2}-2xz" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369892 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369892 1084 #uuid "2c311ac1-0e02-53d0-b880-29d744c3e07c" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369893 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369894 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369893 1069 "q-161912" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369893 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369893 1071 "![](images/26/262fd8eb359ec60654afc5163ad0136851793db70a9f4acdac3f654a3cb5b70c.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F=⟨y,\\,0,\\,x⟩$ and the closed surface $S$ that represents the boundary of the solid shown above. Let $D$ be the projection of the solid onto the $xy$-plane. The flux of $F$ across $S$ can be expressed in terms of a double integral as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∬}_{D}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be the missing expression?" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369893 1072 #uuid "41ee25e9-f08d-5fc1-8dd4-978823d88553" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369893 1074 "Since we have a closed surface, the positive orientation is outward-pointing by convention. So,\n\n- the upper surface ${S}_{1}:z=g(x,y)=0$ is oriented upward, and\n\n- the lower surface ${S}_{2}:z=h(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4$ is oriented downward.\n\nNow, we write down the flux across each of the surfaces separately.\n\n- Consider the upper plane ${S}_{1}.$ \n\nSince the positive orientation is upward, the unit normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨0,0,1⟩.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨y,0,x⟩\\cdot ⟨0,0,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider the lower paraboloid ${S}_{2}.$\n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=h(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4)=2x \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4)=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP=y,\\,Q=0,\\,R=x.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is downward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & =-{∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂h}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂h}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(-y\\cdot 2x-0\\cdot 2y+x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2xy-x\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux across the entire surface is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S+{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}2xy-x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369894 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369895 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369894 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369896 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369894 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369897 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369894 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369898 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369894 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369899 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369894 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369894 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369894 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369896 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369894 1080 #uuid "e9d0f8b6-f6af-5e45-9446-a21fef36eca7" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369895 1081 "y-x" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369895 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 175921860455