that our surface $z=2x+2y$ can be written using the dot product as \n\n$$\n⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩\\cdot {{⟨-2,\\,-2,\\,1⟩}_{⏟}}_{\\overset{~}{n}}=0,\\,\\text{or}\\,⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩\\cdot {{⟨2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩}_{⏟}}_{-\\overset{~}{n}}=0.\n$$\n\nSince we require a downward-pointing normal vector to our surface $S,$ we must select one where the $z$-component is negative. This gives us the normal vector\n\n$$\n\\overset{~}{n}=⟨2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nNormalizing this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{\\overset{~}{n}}{‖\\overset{~}{n}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $z=2x+2y$ on $S,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨3-x,\\,x+y,\\,z-2x⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}⟨2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨3-x,\\,x+y,\\,2y⟩\\cdot ⟨2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(2(3-x)+2(x+y)-2y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(6-2x+2x+2y-2y) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the flux of $F$ across $S$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}2\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & =2{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\text{Area}(S) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369901 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369902 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369901 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369903 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369901 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369904 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369901 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369905 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369901 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369906 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369901 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369901 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369901 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369904 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369901 1080 #uuid "c2c2c4c4-1b4d-5931