r surface $S,$ we must select one where the $z$-component is negative. This gives us the normal vector\n\n$$\n\\overset{~}{n}=⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nNormalizing this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{\\overset{~}{n}}{‖\\overset{~}{n}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $z=x-y+2$ on $S,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨x,\\,-3y,\\,z⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨x,\\,-3y,\\,x-y+2⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}(x+3y-(x-y+2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}(4y-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the flux of $F$ across $S$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}(4y-2)\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}(4y-2)\\cdot ||{r}_{x}\\times {r}_{y}||\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}(4y-2)\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\sqrt{3}}}(4y-2)\\cdot \\cancel{\\sqrt{3}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(4y-2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(4y-2)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}(4y-2)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[x]_{0}^{3}\\cdot {[2{y}^{2}-2y]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369915 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369916 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369915 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369917 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369915 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369918 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369915 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369919 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369915 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369920 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369915 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369915 1077 "sele