 ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}{x}^{2}\\cdot 5Mx\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{x}^{3}y]}_{y=0}^{y={x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5M{[\\frac{1}{7}{x}^{7}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =5M\\cdot \\frac{1}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{5M}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{5M}{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369944 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369945 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369946 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369947 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369943 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369948 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369943 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369943 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369943 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369944 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369943 1080 #uuid "389c7304-cde4-5e40-a3