us of gyration of the plate about the $x$-axis." 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369949 1072 #uuid "067d7788-9583-5931-934f-e2fcc0afe2cd" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369949 1074 "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nIn polar coordinates, the region occupied by the plate is given by\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 2,\\,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{3\\pi }{4}}.\n$$\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (r,\\theta )$ is the mass density function.\n\nAlso, the mass density in terms of polar coordinates is $\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{M}{2r{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }.$\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta ){r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}({\\int }_{1}^{2}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{r}^{3}{|}_{1}^{2}\\cdot \\theta {|}_{\\pi /4}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{7}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi M}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{x} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{7\\pi M}{12}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{7\\pi }{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369951 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369952 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369953 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369954 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369950 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369955 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369950 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369950 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369950 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369955 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369950 1080 #uuid "830fee00-f820-56a3-8ac9-9fc9427d0db6" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369951 1081 "\\sqrt{\\frac{5\\pi }{6}}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369951 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369951 1084 #uuid "e0262f9a-c23f-5c35-a027-03b3fc81a75c" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369952 1081 "3\\sqrt{\\frac{5\\pi }{2}}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369952 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369952 1084 #uuid "9f361312-5827-5b0a-b58d-b9eddb41de0b" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369953 1081 "\\sqrt{\\frac{7\\pi }{5}}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369953 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369953 1084 #uuid "8c081c70-f75d-5718-b946-60bbec11cfd6" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369954 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{3\\pi }{2}}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369954 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369954 1084 #uuid "1a6e95a5-bbc3-5d39-9bea-68dc8e2271a2" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369955 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\frac{7\\pi }{3}}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369955 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369955 1084 #uuid "ca3a5ea2-b4a2-57a3-98b1-a1d0ab4c08f9" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369956 1068 #edb/ref 17592186369957 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369956 1069 "q-164540" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369956 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369956 1071 "The vector-valued function $f(r,\\theta ),$ given by\n\n$$\nf(r,\\theta )=⟨{r}^{2},\\,\\text{_____},\\,4r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩\n$$\n\nparametrizes the elliptic paraboloid defined in Cartesian coordinates as\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}.\n$$\n\nBy first considering the transformations\n\n$$\nx=Z,\\,y=3X,\\,z=4Y\n$$\n\nand writing the resulting system in cylindrical polar coordinates, determine the second component of $f.$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369956 1072 #uuid "e4888437-fd02-5214-b8cd-f906df6dfc66" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369956 1074 "First, substituting the transformations\n\n$$\nx=Z,\\,y=3X,\\,z=4Y\n$$\n\ninto our equation, we get\n\n$$\nZ={X}^{2}+{Y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical coordinates of a point and $(X,Y,Z)$ are the corresponding Cartesian coordinates of that point, then we have\n\n$$\nX=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,Y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,Z=z.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z & ={X}^{2}+{Y}^{2} \\\\ Z & =(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2} \\\\ Z & ={r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ Z & ={r}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r,\\theta ) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨Z,3X,4Y⟩ \\\\  & =⟨Z,\\,3r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,4r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{r}^{2},\\,3r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,4r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $r\\in [0,\\infty )$ and $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is $3r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369958 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369959 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369960 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369961 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369957 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369962 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369957 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369957 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369957 1079 #edb/ref 17592186369958 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369957 1080 #uuid "18208fa2-3a2f-5228-bbdd-c002b56d7270" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369958 1081 "3r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369958 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369958 1084 #uuid "c6a5dadf-34f5-5c68-b377-e69c51ce391f" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369959 1081 "3\\sqrt{r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369959 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369959 1084 #uuid "abb7a386-0955-5c9a-b672-e3a0b4a78970" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369960 1081 "3r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369960 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369960 1084 #uuid "acfa0702-979f-5d40-a79e-b5e5c7191c2c" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369961 1081 "\\frac{9}{4}r\\operator