 ,\\,Z=Z.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}^{2}+{Y}^{2}-{Z}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}-{Z}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )-{Z}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {r}^{2}-{Z}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {Z}^{2}-{r}^{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, the hyperbola ${Z}^{2}-{r}^{2}=1$ represents the intersection of our hyperboloid with the plane that passes through the $Z$-axis and makes the angle of $\\theta $ with the positive $X$-axis. Using the hint, a parametrization of such hyperbola can be given as\n\n$$\n⟨Z,r⟩=⟨\\operatorname{cosh}⁡ϕ,\\,\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ⟩,\\,ϕ\\in R.\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\theta ,ϕ) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6Z,Y,5X⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6Z,\\,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,5r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6\\operatorname{cosh}⁡ϕ,\\,(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,5(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6\\operatorname{cosh}⁡ϕ,\\,\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,5\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ and $ϕ\\in R.$\n\nTherefore, the third component of $f$ is $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369964 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369965 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369964 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369966 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369964 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369967 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369964 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369968 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369964 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369969 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369964 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369964 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186369964 1079 #edb/ref 17592186