6370624 1072 #uuid "c023a473-9d6e-5414-a840-01ccd5fbe04f" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370624 1074 "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[0,6]$ and differentiable on $(0,6),$  hence we can apply the mean value theorem.  \n\nSo, the mean value theorem states that there exists a $c\\in (0,6)$ such that\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $a=0$ and $b=6$ into the above gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(6)-f(0)}{6-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{({6}^{2}-4\\cdot 6+2)-({0}^{2}-4\\cdot 0+2)}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{14-2}{6} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-4x+2)=2x-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=2c-4.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2c-4 & =2 \\\\ c & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370625 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370626 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370625 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370625 1077 "field-1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370625 1079 #edb/ref 17592186370626 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370625 1080 #uuid "1f74fae6-52cf-5d92-94d3-a3caaa944e7d" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370626 1081 "3" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370626 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370626 1084 #uuid "b6387cd6-97ae-5bb6-9167-2b2c1e0a118f" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370627 1068 #edb/ref 17592186370628 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370627 1069 "q-346591" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370627 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370627 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(x+1)^{9}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370627 1072 #uuid "33e3355d-955a-5955-a1cd-54387f01dc2b" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370627 1074 "First, we substitute $u=x+1.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $x\\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=x+1$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(x+1)^{9}}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{9}}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(x+1)^{9}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{9}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{u}^{-9/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{u}^{-9/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{2}{7}{u}^{-7/2}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{7}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{u}^{-7/2}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{7}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\frac{1}{{a}^{7/2}}-\\frac{1}{{1}^{7/2}}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{7}\\cdot (0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370628 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370629 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370628 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370628 1077 "field-1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370628 1079 #edb/ref 17592186370629 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370628 1080 #uuid "edbc9163-b55c-5bce-840b-693a8baab0a4" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370629 1081 "\\frac{2}{7}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370629 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [175921863706