bills. If one bill is randomly drawn from a bag, what is its expected value?" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370952 1072 #uuid "3b33e7f8-97bd-52b2-9fc5-eb73c2b2d7ec" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370952 1074 "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the value of a randomly drawn bill. Then the support is $S={5,10,20}.$\n\nIn the bag there are  $4$ five-dollar bills, $8$ ten-dollar bills and $6$ twenty-dollar bills (eighteen bills in total), so the probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5) & =\\frac{4}{18}=\\frac{2}{9} \\\\ P(10) & =\\frac{8}{18}=\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ P(20) & =\\frac{6}{18}=\\frac{3}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =5\\cdot f(5)+10\\cdot f(10)+20\\cdot f(20) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{2}{9})+10(\\frac{4}{9})+20(\\frac{3}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{9}+\\frac{40}{9}+\\frac{60}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{10+40+60}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{110}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370953 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370954 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370953 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370955 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370953 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370956 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370953 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370957 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370953 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370958 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370953 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370953 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370953 1079 #edb/ref 17592186370957 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370953 1080 #uuid "45d39d50-e814-58b3-b920-cbbb549d00fb" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370954 1081 "20" 13194139533449 175921860