ef 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370983 1084 #uuid "60cdb5ed-9520-5f38-9c72-9a4ee90513eb" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370984 1081 "y(x)={x}^{3}+3x" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370984 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370984 1084 #uuid "5647fa9f-f8a1-5355-958d-ac9f76d96fcd" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370985 1068 #edb/ref 17592186370986 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370985 1069 "q-64841" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370985 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370985 1071 "Find the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+8x{y}^{′}-3y=0,\\,y(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=2,\\,x>0.\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370985 1072 #uuid "7fa70513-33ac-562e-accc-6e741a539b11" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370985 1074 "Note that the given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}+8x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}-3{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ 4\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }+8\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }-3{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[4\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+8\\lambda -3] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+8\\lambda -3 & =0 \\\\ 4{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda -3 & =0 \\\\ (2\\lambda -1)(2\\lambda +3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the roots are $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\lambda =-\\frac{3}{2}.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{1/2}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-3/2}.\n$$\n\nNow let's find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$\n\nSubstituting $y(1)=0$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n0={c}_{1}+{c}_{2}\\,⇒\\,{c}_{2}=-{c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=2.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{{c}_{1}{x}^{-1/2}}{2}-\\frac{3{c}_{2}{x}^{-5/2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{{c}_{1}}{2}-\\frac{3{c}_{2}}{2} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{{c}_{1}}{2}-\\frac{3(-{c}_{1})}{2} \\\\ 2 & =2{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{1} & =1\\,⇒\\,{c}_{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(x)={x}^{1/2}-{x}^{-3/2}.\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370987 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370988 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370989 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370990 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370986 1075 #edb/ref 17592186370991 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370986 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370986 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370986 1079 #edb/ref 17592186370991 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370986 1080 #uuid "c8d3595b-7aa5-5180-9aed-06125c911386" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370987 1081 "y(x)={x}^{3/2}+{x}^{-1/2}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370987 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370987 1084 #uuid "64f9155f-b8e2-56b7-a158-a740a6de2702" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370988 1081 "y(x)=-2{x}^{-3/2}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370988 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186370988 1084 #uuid "f262bd61-3dc4-5968-8c17-fd17918dc225" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [175921863