 [17592186371006 1071 "Consider a vector-valued function $f(u)$ that is continuous over all real numbers and the real-valued function $u(t)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-t).$ Then ${lim}_{t\\to 0}f(u(t))=$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371006 1072 #uuid "15bc3e4f-0924-5f8f-8c65-4286b13d3aa0" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371006 1074 "First, notice that $u(t)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-t)$ is continuous at $t=0$ and \n\n$$\nu(0)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0)=1.\n$$\n\nSince $f(u)$ is continuous at $u=1$ and $u(t)$ is continuous at $t=0,$ the function $f(u(t))$ is also continuous at $t=0.$\n\nTherefore,\n${lim}_{t\\to 0}f(u(t))=f(u(0))=f(1).$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371007 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371008 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371007 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371009 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371007 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371010 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371007 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371011 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371007 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371012 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371007 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371007 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371007 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371012 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371007 1080 #uuid "98fc209b-8ec5-5bda-97dd-9a6ca3c0cc51" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371008 1081 "f(3)" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371008 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371008 1084 #uuid "619188a5-4b4d-54c0-a9ff-01f17f5b5614" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371009 1081 "f(0)" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371009 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371009 1084 #uuid "c2860fd8-13f3-589e-8c0f-da5c2dac5ec6" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371010 1081 