 vector function $g(t)$ is differentiable on the common domain where its components are differentiable.  \n\nLet's now find the intervals where each of the functions $u(t)$ and $g(t)$ are differentiable. \n\nFor the real-valued function $u(t):$  \n\n- We observe that $u(t)$  is differentiable on $(-1,1),$ as its derivative is not defined at $t=\\pm 1$ and the function is not defined for $|t|>1.$\n\nFor the function $g(t):$ \n\n- The first component, $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\pi t)$,  is not defined for integer values of $t$ and hence it is not differentiable at $t=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,….$\n\n- The second and third components,   $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi t)$ and $1-{t}^{2},$ are differentiable for all values of $t.$\n\nFinally, the common domain of differentiability for $u(t)$ and $g(t)$ is $(-1,0)\\cup (0,1).$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371049 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371050 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371049 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371051 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371049 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371052 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371049 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371053 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371049 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371054 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371049 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371049 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371049 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371051 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371049 1080 #uuid "c4a97578-6664-5343-9ce7-7d7f5bc871f0" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371050 1081 "(-\\infty ,-1)" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371050 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371050 1084 #uuid "9b18481b-fa9c-5c81-ab8a-a8554b782718" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371051 1081 "(-1,0)\\cup (0,1)" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371051 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 