 integral ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-2x+1.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{4x}-2x+1.\n$$\n\nNow let's find the constants $A$ and $B.$ \n\nSubstituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA+B=1.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=8.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-2A{e}^{-2x}+4B{e}^{4x}-2\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=8$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-2A+4B=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following system of equations for $A$ and $B:$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}A+B=1 \\\\ -2A+4B=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $A=-1,B=2.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-{e}^{-2x}+2{e}^{4x}-2x+1.\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371098 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371099 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371098 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371100 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371098 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371101 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371098 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371102 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371098 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371103 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371098 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371098 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371098 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371099 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371098 1080 #uuid "ca78cc66-c01e-58dd-9a61-3727fb6f5bbd" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371099 1081 "y=-{e}^{-2x}+2{e}^{4x}-2x+1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371099 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371099 1084 #uuid "c99d53a9-e3cd-5940-92bd-1ac167fee043" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371100 1081 "y=-3{e}^{-2x}-{e}^{4x}+3x+2" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371100 1083 #edb/r