erivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=2\\alpha x+\\beta ,\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=2\\alpha \n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta $ and $\\gamma ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n2\\alpha +4(2\\alpha x+\\beta )+3(\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma )=3{x}^{2}+2x+3\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives:\n\n$$\n3\\alpha {x}^{2}+(8\\alpha +3\\beta )x+(2\\alpha +4\\beta +3\\gamma )=3{x}^{2}+2x+3\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3\\alpha =3\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,{x}^{2}) \\\\ 8\\alpha +3\\beta =2\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ 2\\alpha +4\\beta +3\\gamma =3\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =1,\\beta =-2,\\gamma =3.$\n\nTherefore, the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x)$ is:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={x}^{2}-2x+3\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371105 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371106 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371105 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371107 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371105 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371108 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371105 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371109 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371105 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371110 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371105 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371105 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371105 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371110 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371105 1080 #uuid "5fd83c91-8d54-5d91-bd2e-603f01529164" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371106 1081 "{y}_{p}(x)=2{x}^{2}+2x+1" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371106 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371106 