gned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}=1 \\\\ {v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}=1 \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{2}{5}=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{4}{5}=1 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{1}{5}=1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $U$ is orthonormal.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=0+1=1\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$U$ only\"." 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371141 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371142 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371143 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [1