X$ be a roll of an unfair four-sided die that follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the standard deviation of $X?$\n\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371152 1072 #uuid "1e518a99-0566-5086-b5fd-28824f354071" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371152 1074 "The standard deviation of a random variable $X$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]},\n$$\n\nwhere the variance can be computed using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{6})+2(\\frac{1}{3})+3(\\frac{1}{6})+4(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{4}^{2}\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{6})+4(\\frac{1}{3})+9(\\frac{1}{6})+16(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{3}-{(\\frac{8}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{3}-\\frac{64}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371154 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371155 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [1759