" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371159 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371159 1071 "Several egg cartons were checked for cracked eggs. The number of cracked eggs in each carton was recorded below. Based on this data, if the random variable $N$ represents the number of cracked eggs in a randomly selected carton, what is $\\text{SD}[N]?$\n\n| Number of Cartons | $3$ | $8$ | $5$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Cracked Eggs | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371159 1072 #uuid "174acb17-be7e-55d6-b6f6-0012762f5d63" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371159 1074 "The standard deviation of a random variable $N$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[N]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[N]},\n$$\n\nwhere the variance can be computed using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[N]=\\text{E}[{N}^{2}]-\\text{E}[N]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute the probability mass function $f(n).$ To do this, we divide each frequency by the total, which is $3+8+5+4=20.$ We get the following result:\n\n| $f(n)$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $n$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n\nNow, we compute $\\text{E}[N]$ by summing up the products of each value of $N$ and its associated probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[N] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0+(\\frac{2}{5})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[{N}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${N}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{N}^{2}] & ={0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0+(\\frac{2}{5})+4(\\frac{1}{4})+9(\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[N] & =\\text{E}[{N}^{2}]-\\text{E}[N]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{5}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{5}-\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[N] & =\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[N]} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{19}{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{2\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{95}}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371160 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371161 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371160 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371162 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371160 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371163 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371160 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371164 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371160 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371165 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371160 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371160 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371160 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371163 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371160 1080 #uuid "7f9ee19a-28cd-535c-8d83-c4ed471717aa" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371161 1081 "\\frac{\\sqrt{65}}{6}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371161 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371161 1084 #uuid "0151266b-668a-5320-8a65-9d7c491f3a8f" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371162 1081 "\\frac{\\sqrt{65}}{8}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371162 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371162 1084 #uuid "2dd5e7df-4a9a-5c14-bb4c-d2b3137cc052" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371163 1081 "\\frac{\\sqrt{95}}{10}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371163 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371163 1084 #uuid "a1f690b4-c4fa-5a65-93db-4006f004e699" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371164 1081 "\\frac{\\sqrt{45}}{5}" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371164 1083 #edb/