b/ref 17592186371208 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371207 1069 "q-84066" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371207 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371207 1071 "A stack of cards has $8$ cards labeled with three and $4$ cards labeled with six. If one card is randomly drawn from the stack,  what is its expected value?" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371207 1072 #uuid "18b2f834-79d8-5108-ac3b-be3414d6b074" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371207 1074 "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the value labeled on a randomly drawn card. Then the support is $S={3,6}.$\n\nIn the stack there are $8$ cards labeled with three and $4$ cards labeled with six (twelve cards in total), so the probabilities are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3) & =\\frac{8}{12}=\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ P(6) & =\\frac{4}{12}=\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =3\\cdot f(3)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{2}{3})+6(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =2+2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371208 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371209 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371208 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371210 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371208 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371211 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371208 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371212 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371208 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371213 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371208 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371208 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371208 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371211 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371208 1080 #uuid "80840b6f-2c49-52de-971e-fcf8f409c87e" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371209 1081 "3" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371209 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371209 1084 #uuid "a5666759-5b7a-5feb-b09b-583e04b7dbee" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371210 1081 "4.5" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371210 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371210 1084 #uuid "99dc09b7-d225-576b-9d4b-f00fdffe5d08" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371211 1081 "4" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371211 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371211 1084 #uuid "a0f22dff-ce12-5116-bb53-0f6b17fff1df" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371212 1081 "3.5" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371212 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371212 1084 #uuid "a2074e86-d25f-5eb9-b87c-922818636eae" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371213 1081 "5" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371213 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371213 1084 #uuid "f7c7cd85-1bac-512f-aa0f-71b474d98603" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371214 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371215 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371214 1069 "q-84200" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371214 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371214 1071 "Let $X$ be the number obtained by a spinner with six sections labeled $1,2,3,4,5,6.$ The probability mass function $f(x)$ of $X$ is shown in the table below. What is $\\text{Var}[X]?$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ |" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371214 1072 #uuid "c3a58674-a3cd-5ee4-b896-c22541ee7460" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371214 1074 "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{8})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{3}{8})+4(\\frac{1}{16})+5(\\frac{1}{8})+6(\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{4}^{2}\\cdot f(4)+{5}^{2}\\cdot f(5)+{6}^{2}\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{8})+4(\\frac{1}{4})+9(\\frac{3}{8})+16(\\frac{1}{16})+25(\\frac{1}{8})+36(\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{87}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{87}{8}-{3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{87}{8}-9 \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371215 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371216 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371215 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371217 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371215 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371218 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371215 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371219 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371215 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371220 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371215 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371215 1077 "selection" 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371215 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371218 13194139533449 17592186045585 true] [17592186371215 1080 #uuid "21a9ba9e-cc38-50be-a